{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"gpu","dataSources":[],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"9c7390db-00fd-42f7-a062-2a9b147039ac","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Context Curation as a Lightweight Defense Against Distribution Shift in Tabular Foundation Models\n\n**v2 — extended with a retraining baseline, a real-drift dataset, a reweighted-calibration baseline,\nshift-detectability diagnostics, three ablations, and an explanation-stability (XAI) study.**\n\n**Research question:** TabPFN-style tabular foundation models predict by conditioning on a *context* of\nlabeled training rows, with no gradient updates. Existing shift-robust variants (e.g. Drift-Resilient\nTabPFN) handle distribution shift by **retraining the pretraining prior** — expensive, and it discards\nTabPFN's main advantage (fast, zero-training inference). This notebook asks:\n\n> **Can smarter selection of which rows go into the context — decided at inference time, with no\n> retraining, using only unlabeled target features — recover most of the robustness benefit that full\n> retraining buys you?**\n\nFully self-contained, designed to run top-to-bottom on Kaggle (GPU recommended; CPU works for the\nsmaller datasets). What it produces, end to end:\n\n1. **Main grid**: 5 datasets × 3 synthetic shift types × 4 severities × 5 context strategies × context\n   sizes × seeds, run through TabPFN, scored on accuracy / ROC-AUC / ECE / Brier.\n2. **Reference baselines**: full-data XGBoost, RandomForest, LightGBM, *importance-weighted* XGBoost\n   (the actual \"what if you retrained instead\" comparison), and TabPFN + reweighted post-hoc\n   calibration (the \"what if you recalibrated instead\" comparison).\n3. **A real-world drift case study**: the Electricity (elec2) dataset, split chronologically — genuine\n   concept drift, not synthetic.\n4. **Mechanism analysis**: does context curation help more when a cheap domain-classifier AUC says the\n   shift is more severe?\n5. **Three ablations**: context size, how much unlabeled target data you actually need, and whether the\n   domain-classifier choice for `shift_aware_context` matters.\n6. **Explanation stability (XAI)**: does shift-aware context also stabilize *which features the model\n   relies on*, not just its accuracy, when the data shifts?\n\n**If something breaks:** every experiment cell logs failures into the results table (`status=\"failed\"`,\nwith the error message) instead of crashing. Send me `results_raw.csv` / the printed failure log and\nI'll fix the specific cell — no need to re-run everything.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"efc680ee-47db-40ba-9033-9f2cae35dcd6","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 0. Setup","metadata":{}},{"id":"80677476-223d-4925-9a0f-89fc1c071cd8","cell_type":"code","source":"import sys, subprocess\n\ndef pip_install(pkg):\n    subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"-q\", pkg], check=False)\n\nfor pkg in [\"tabpfn\", \"scikit-learn\", \"xgboost\", \"lightgbm\", \"scipy\", \"matplotlib\", \"seaborn\", \"pandas\"]:\n    pip_install(pkg)\n\nprint(\"Install step done.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-12T21:08:18.518078Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-12T21:08:18.51834Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-12T21:08:46.425967Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-12T21:08:18.51831Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-12T21:08:46.425097Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"   ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 732.3/732.3 kB 34.7 MB/s eta 0:00:00\nInstall step done.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"id":"1c8702d6-ce73-451c-878d-725f1cb7cd96","cell_type":"code","source":"import os\nOFFLINE_WEIGHTS_DIR = \"/kaggle/input/tabpfn-2-5/pytorch/default/2\"  # edit if your dataset slug differs\nif os.path.isdir(OFFLINE_WEIGHTS_DIR):\n    os.environ[\"TABPFN_MODEL_CACHE_DIR\"] = OFFLINE_WEIGHTS_DIR\n    print(f\"Using offline TabPFN weights from {OFFLINE_WEIGHTS_DIR}\")\nelse:\n    print(\"No offline weights dir found — TabPFN will try to auto-download on first use \"\n          \"(needs internet + accepting the license once).\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-12T21:08:46.427593Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-12T21:08:46.428046Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-12T21:08:46.432903Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-12T21:08:46.42802Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-12T21:08:46.432062Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"No offline weights dir found — TabPFN will try to auto-download on first use (needs internet + accepting the license once).\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"id":"fe700e02-d80f-4321-8b6c-898e822c38d3","cell_type":"code","source":"import warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n\nimport time\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nfrom sklearn.datasets import fetch_openml\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OrdinalEncoder\nfrom sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\nfrom sklearn.cluster import KMeans\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_score\nfrom sklearn.inspection import permutation_importance\nfrom sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, roc_auc_score, brier_score_loss\n\nimport xgboost as xgb\nimport lightgbm as lgb\n\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport seaborn as sns\nsns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n\nSEED = 42\nnp.random.seed(SEED)\n\nRESULTS_PATH = \"results_raw.csv\"\nFIG_DIR = \"figures\"\nos.makedirs(FIG_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\nprint(\"Imports OK\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-12T21:08:46.433895Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-12T21:08:46.434179Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-12T21:08:53.48886Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-12T21:08:46.43415Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-12T21:08:53.487864Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Imports OK\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"id":"26df714c-8ba9-41f8-b4ac-449d6c5af306","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Datasets\n\nFive public binary-classification tabular datasets. Four use **synthetic controlled shift** (so we can\nsweep severity cleanly); the fifth, **Electricity (elec2)**, is a genuine real-world concept-drift\nbenchmark used chronologically in Section 6b — this is what lets the paper claim results aren't just an\nartifact of how the synthetic shifts were built.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"72c8aabf-5666-4c43-9fff-39812b6f513b","cell_type":"code","source":"@dataclass\nclass DatasetSpec:\n    name: str\n    openml_name: str\n    openml_version: int\n    target: str\n    shift_feature: str\n    positive_label: Optional[str] = None\n    time_cols: Optional[list] = None   # for datasets usable in the real chronological-shift study\n\nDATASETS = [\n    DatasetSpec(\"adult_income\", \"adult\", 2, \"class\", \"age\", \">50K\"),\n    DatasetSpec(\"german_credit\", \"credit-g\", 1, \"class\", \"age\", \"good\"),\n    DatasetSpec(\"bank_marketing\", \"bank-marketing\", 1, \"Class\", \"V1\", \"2\"),\n    DatasetSpec(\"diabetes\", \"diabetes\", 1, \"class\", \"age\", \"tested_positive\"),\n    DatasetSpec(\"electricity\", \"electricity\", 1, \"class\", \"nswdemand\", \"UP\", time_cols=[\"date\", \"period\"]),\n]\n\ndef load_dataset(spec: DatasetSpec, max_rows: int = 15000):\n    data = fetch_openml(name=spec.openml_name, version=spec.openml_version, as_frame=True, parser=\"auto\")\n    df = data.frame.copy()\n    if spec.target not in df.columns:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Target column {spec.target} not found in {spec.openml_name}; \"\n                          f\"available columns: {list(df.columns)}\")\n\n    y_raw = df[spec.target]\n    if spec.positive_label is not None:\n        y = (y_raw.astype(str) == str(spec.positive_label)).astype(int).values\n    else:\n        y = y_raw.astype(int).values\n\n    X = df.drop(columns=[spec.target])\n\n    # keep original row order (needed for electricity's chronological structure) before any subsampling\n    if len(X) > max_rows:\n        if spec.time_cols:\n            # keep a contiguous, chronologically-ordered slice rather than a random subsample\n            start = np.random.RandomState(SEED).randint(0, max(1, len(X) - max_rows))\n            X = X.iloc[start:start + max_rows].reset_index(drop=True)\n            y = y[start:start + max_rows]\n        else:\n            idx = np.random.RandomState(SEED).choice(len(X), size=max_rows, replace=False)\n            X = X.iloc[idx].reset_index(drop=True)\n            y = y[idx]\n\n    if spec.shift_feature not in X.columns:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Shift feature {spec.shift_feature} not in columns for {spec.openml_name}: \"\n                          f\"{list(X.columns)}\")\n\n    return X, y\n\ndef preprocess(X: pd.DataFrame):\n    X = X.copy()\n    cat_cols = X.select_dtypes(include=[\"category\", \"object\"]).columns.tolist()\n    num_cols = [c for c in X.columns if c not in cat_cols]\n\n    if cat_cols:\n        X[cat_cols] = X[cat_cols].astype(str)\n        enc = OrdinalEncoder(handle_unknown=\"use_encoded_value\", unknown_value=-1)\n        X[cat_cols] = enc.fit_transform(X[cat_cols])\n\n    imputer = SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")\n    X[:] = imputer.fit_transform(X)\n\n    scaler = StandardScaler()\n    if num_cols:\n        X[num_cols] = scaler.fit_transform(X[num_cols])\n\n    return X.values.astype(np.float32), X.columns.tolist()\n\nprint(\"Dataset loader ready.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-12T21:08:53.489877Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-12T21:08:53.490388Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-12T21:08:53.502011Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-12T21:08:53.490363Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-12T21:08:53.501312Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Dataset loader ready.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":4},{"id":"58f05e1e-af80-4ad2-b3a6-9c58006f685e","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Shift construction\n\nSame three synthetic shift types as before (covariate / label / feature-noise, severity in `[0, 1]`),\nplus a new `split_chronological` used only for the Electricity real-drift case study in Section 6b:\ntrain on an earlier contiguous window, test on a later one, with `severity` controlling how far forward\nin time the test window sits (natural concept drift, not constructed).\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"b995b62d-462e-4aab-98e4-d04e33612275","cell_type":"code","source":"def split_covariate_shift(X, y, shift_vals, severity, test_size=0.3, seed=SEED):\n    order = np.argsort(shift_vals)\n    X, y, shift_vals = X[order], y[order], shift_vals[order]\n    n = len(X)\n    n_test = int(n * test_size)\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n    if severity <= 0:\n        idx = rng.permutation(n)\n        test_idx, train_idx = idx[:n_test], idx[n_test:]\n    else:\n        sorted_test_idx = np.arange(n - n_test, n)\n        rand_idx = rng.permutation(n)\n        rand_test_idx = rand_idx[:n_test]\n        n_from_sorted = int(round(severity * n_test))\n        test_idx = np.concatenate([sorted_test_idx[:n_from_sorted], rand_test_idx[: n_test - n_from_sorted]])\n        test_idx = np.unique(test_idx)[:n_test]\n        train_idx = np.setdiff1d(np.arange(n), test_idx)\n    return X[train_idx], y[train_idx], X[test_idx], y[test_idx]\n\n\ndef split_label_shift(X, y, severity, test_size=0.3, seed=SEED):\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n    idx = rng.permutation(len(X))\n    n_test = int(len(X) * test_size)\n    test_idx, train_idx = idx[:n_test], idx[n_test:]\n    X_train, y_train = X[train_idx], y[train_idx]\n    X_test, y_test = X[test_idx], y[test_idx]\n\n    train_pos_rate = y_train.mean()\n    target_pos_rate = np.clip(train_pos_rate * (1 - severity) + (1 - train_pos_rate) * severity, 0.05, 0.95)\n\n    pos_idx = np.where(y_test == 1)[0]\n    neg_idx = np.where(y_test == 0)[0]\n    n_pos_target = int(round(target_pos_rate * len(test_idx)))\n    n_neg_target = len(test_idx) - n_pos_target\n    pos_sample = rng.choice(pos_idx, size=min(n_pos_target, len(pos_idx)), replace=len(pos_idx) < n_pos_target)\n    neg_sample = rng.choice(neg_idx, size=min(n_neg_target, len(neg_idx)), replace=len(neg_idx) < n_neg_target)\n    keep = np.concatenate([pos_sample, neg_sample])\n    rng.shuffle(keep)\n    return X_train, y_train, X_test[keep], y_test[keep]\n\n\ndef split_feature_noise_shift(X, y, severity, test_size=0.3, seed=SEED, max_noise_std=2.0):\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n    idx = rng.permutation(len(X))\n    n_test = int(len(X) * test_size)\n    test_idx, train_idx = idx[:n_test], idx[n_test:]\n    X_train, y_train = X[train_idx], y[train_idx]\n    X_test, y_test = X[test_idx].copy(), y[test_idx]\n    noise = rng.normal(0, severity * max_noise_std, size=X_test.shape).astype(np.float32)\n    return X_train, y_train, X_test + noise, y_test\n\n\ndef split_chronological(X, y, severity, train_frac=0.4, test_size=0.2, seed=SEED):\n    \"\"\"Assumes X, y are already in chronological row order (true for Electricity as loaded above).\n    severity=0 -> test window starts right after train window ends.\n    severity=1 -> test window is drawn from the far end of the dataset (max temporal gap).\"\"\"\n    n = len(X)\n    n_train = int(n * train_frac)\n    n_test = int(n * test_size)\n    max_start = n - n_test\n    min_start = n_train\n    test_start = int(min_start + severity * max(0, (max_start - min_start)))\n    test_start = min(test_start, max_start)\n    train_idx = np.arange(0, n_train)\n    test_idx = np.arange(test_start, test_start + n_test)\n    return X[train_idx], y[train_idx], X[test_idx], y[test_idx]\n\nSHIFT_BUILDERS = {\n    \"covariate\": split_covariate_shift,\n    \"label\": split_label_shift,\n    \"feature_noise\": split_feature_noise_shift,\n}\nSEVERITIES = [0.0, 0.3, 0.6, 1.0]\n\nprint(\"Shift builders ready.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-12T21:09:27.773521Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-12T21:09:27.773804Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-12T21:09:27.787361Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-12T21:09:27.773763Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-12T21:09:27.786454Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Shift builders ready.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":6},{"id":"9e5edb02-f691-48a0-9c8b-354b2f048790","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Context-selection strategies\n\nUnchanged core logic from v1, with `shift_aware_context` now calling a shared `compute_domain_weights`\nhelper (Section 4) so the exact same weights can be reused by the importance-weighted retraining\nbaseline and the reweighted-calibration baseline — this matters for the paper: it means \"context\ncuration\" and \"retraining\" are being given *the same shift signal*, so any performance gap between them\nis attributable to the mechanism, not to one method having a better shift estimate than the other.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"94562a20-8811-4e6a-9690-f921f3a05808","cell_type":"code","source":"def random_context(X_train, y_train, X_target_unlabeled, context_size, seed=SEED, **kw):\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n    idx = rng.choice(len(X_train), size=min(context_size, len(X_train)), replace=False)\n    return idx\n\ndef class_balanced_context(X_train, y_train, X_target_unlabeled, context_size, seed=SEED, **kw):\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n    classes = np.unique(y_train)\n    per_class = context_size // len(classes)\n    idx_parts = []\n    for c in classes:\n        c_idx = np.where(y_train == c)[0]\n        take = min(per_class, len(c_idx))\n        idx_parts.append(rng.choice(c_idx, size=take, replace=False))\n    idx = np.concatenate(idx_parts)\n    rng.shuffle(idx)\n    return idx[:context_size]\n\ndef knn_context(X_train, y_train, X_target_unlabeled, context_size, seed=SEED, **kw):\n    centroid = X_target_unlabeled.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(context_size, len(X_train))).fit(X_train)\n    _, idx = nn.kneighbors(centroid)\n    return idx[0]\n\ndef diversity_context(X_train, y_train, X_target_unlabeled, context_size, seed=SEED, **kw):\n    k = min(context_size, len(X_train))\n    km = KMeans(n_clusters=k, n_init=3, random_state=seed).fit(X_train)\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=1).fit(X_train)\n    _, idx = nn.kneighbors(km.cluster_centers_)\n    return np.unique(idx.ravel())[:context_size]\n\ndef compute_domain_weights(X_train, X_target_unlabeled, seed=SEED, domain_clf_type=\"logreg\"):\n    \"\"\"Trains a domain classifier to separate X_train from X_target_unlabeled; returns\n    importance weights for each X_train row (higher = more target-like) plus the fitted classifier's\n    3-fold CV AUC as a cheap 'how detectable is this shift' diagnostic.\"\"\"\n    n_train, n_target = len(X_train), len(X_target_unlabeled)\n    domain_X = np.vstack([X_train, X_target_unlabeled])\n    domain_y = np.concatenate([np.zeros(n_train), np.ones(n_target)])\n\n    if domain_clf_type == \"logreg\":\n        clf = LogisticRegression(max_iter=500)\n    elif domain_clf_type == \"random_forest\":\n        clf = RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=200, max_depth=6, random_state=seed, n_jobs=4)\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(domain_clf_type)\n\n    try:\n        cv_auc = cross_val_score(clf, domain_X, domain_y, cv=3, scoring=\"roc_auc\").mean()\n    except Exception:\n        cv_auc = np.nan\n\n    clf.fit(domain_X, domain_y)\n    p_target = np.clip(clf.predict_proba(X_train)[:, 1], 1e-3, 1 - 1e-3)\n    importance_weights = p_target / (1 - p_target)   # density-ratio-style importance weight\n    return importance_weights, cv_auc\n\ndef shift_aware_context(X_train, y_train, X_target_unlabeled, context_size, seed=SEED, domain_clf_type=\"logreg\", **kw):\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n    weights, _ = compute_domain_weights(X_train, X_target_unlabeled, seed=seed, domain_clf_type=domain_clf_type)\n    probs = weights / weights.sum()\n    idx = rng.choice(len(X_train), size=min(context_size, len(X_train)), replace=False, p=probs)\n    return idx\n\nCONTEXT_STRATEGIES = {\n    \"random\": random_context,\n    \"class_balanced\": class_balanced_context,\n    \"knn_to_target\": knn_context,\n    \"diversity_kmeans\": diversity_context,\n    \"shift_aware_reweight\": shift_aware_context,\n}\n\nprint(\"Context strategies ready.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-12T21:09:38.631849Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-12T21:09:38.632308Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-12T21:09:38.645544Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-12T21:09:38.632281Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-12T21:09:38.644935Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Context strategies ready.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":7},{"id":"986b4802-3b58-4b0b-9554-26e699271c06","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Models, baselines, and metrics\n\nReference points now cover three distinct \"alternative strategies\" a practitioner could reach for\ninstead of context curation:\n\n| Baseline | What it represents |\n|---|---|\n| `xgboost_full`, `random_forest_full`, `lightgbm_full` | \"just use a non-foundation-model, trained on everything\" |\n| `xgboost_importance_weighted` | **\"retrain, but shift-aware\"** — same domain-classifier signal as `shift_aware_reweight`, applied as sample weights to a full retrain. This is the key comparison: does context curation get you most of what this costs-more approach buys? |\n| `tabpfn_reweighted_calibration` | **\"don't touch the context, recalibrate instead\"** — TabPFN on a random context, then importance-weighted Platt scaling fit on a held-out labeled slice of the training pool, reweighted toward target-likeness. Represents the calibration-only literature (e.g. AdapTable's spirit, simplified) as a non-context-curation alternative. |\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"d2768625-0834-4e3c-a4d1-47cd11d10895","cell_type":"code","source":"def expected_calibration_error(y_true, y_prob, n_bins=10):\n    bins = np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1)\n    ece, n = 0.0, len(y_true)\n    for i in range(n_bins):\n        lo, hi = bins[i], bins[i + 1]\n        mask = (y_prob >= lo) & (y_prob < hi if i < n_bins - 1 else y_prob <= hi)\n        if mask.sum() == 0:\n            continue\n        ece += (mask.sum() / n) * abs(y_true[mask].mean() - y_prob[mask].mean())\n    return ece\n\ndef score_predictions(y_true, y_prob):\n    y_pred = (y_prob >= 0.5).astype(int)\n    out = {}\n    try: out[\"accuracy\"] = accuracy_score(y_true, y_pred)\n    except Exception: out[\"accuracy\"] = np.nan\n    try: out[\"roc_auc\"] = roc_auc_score(y_true, y_prob) if len(np.unique(y_true)) > 1 else np.nan\n    except Exception: out[\"roc_auc\"] = np.nan\n    try: out[\"ece\"] = expected_calibration_error(y_true, y_prob)\n    except Exception: out[\"ece\"] = np.nan\n    try: out[\"brier\"] = brier_score_loss(y_true, y_prob)\n    except Exception: out[\"brier\"] = np.nan\n    return out\n\ndef _has_cuda():\n    \"\"\"torch.cuda.is_available() can return True even when the installed torch build doesn't\n    actually match the GPU driver Kaggle assigned (a known issue: pip-installing tabpfn can pull in\n    a torch wheel with a mismatched CUDA build, producing 'CUDA error: no kernel image is available\n    for execution on the device' the first time a real op runs, not at import time). So we run a tiny\n    real op and catch failure, instead of trusting is_available() alone.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        import torch\n        if not torch.cuda.is_available():\n            return False\n        _ = (torch.zeros(2, device=\"cuda\") + 1).cpu()\n        return True\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"[device check] CUDA reported available but a test op failed ({type(e).__name__}: {e}); \"\n              f\"falling back to CPU.\")\n        return False\n\n# Computed once, not per TabPFN call — avoids re-running the functional probe hundreds of times.\nTABPFN_DEVICE = \"cuda\" if _has_cuda() else \"cpu\"\nprint(f\"TabPFN will run on: {TABPFN_DEVICE}\")\n\ndef run_tabpfn(X_context, y_context, X_test):\n    from tabpfn import TabPFNClassifier\n    clf = TabPFNClassifier(device=TABPFN_DEVICE)\n    clf.fit(X_context, y_context)\n    return clf.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n\ndef run_xgb_full(X_train, y_train, X_test, **kw):\n    clf = xgb.XGBClassifier(n_estimators=200, max_depth=5, learning_rate=0.1,\n                             eval_metric=\"logloss\", n_jobs=4, random_state=SEED)\n    clf.fit(X_train, y_train)\n    return clf.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n\ndef run_rf_full(X_train, y_train, X_test, **kw):\n    clf = RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=300, n_jobs=4, random_state=SEED)\n    clf.fit(X_train, y_train)\n    return clf.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n\ndef run_lgbm_full(X_train, y_train, X_test, **kw):\n    clf = lgb.LGBMClassifier(n_estimators=300, max_depth=6, learning_rate=0.1,\n                              random_state=SEED, verbosity=-1, n_jobs=4)\n    clf.fit(X_train, y_train)\n    return clf.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n\ndef run_xgb_importance_weighted(X_train, y_train, X_test, X_target_unlabeled=None, seed=SEED, **kw):\n    weights, _ = compute_domain_weights(X_train, X_target_unlabeled, seed=seed)\n    clf = xgb.XGBClassifier(n_estimators=200, max_depth=5, learning_rate=0.1,\n                             eval_metric=\"logloss\", n_jobs=4, random_state=SEED)\n    clf.fit(X_train, y_train, sample_weight=weights)\n    return clf.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n\ndef run_tabpfn_reweighted_calibration(X_train, y_train, X_target_unlabeled, X_score, context_size, seed=SEED, **kw):\n    \"\"\"TabPFN on a random context, then importance-weighted Platt scaling fit on a held-out labeled\n    slice of the training pool (never touches target labels).\"\"\"\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n    idx = rng.permutation(len(X_train))\n    n_cal = max(50, int(0.2 * len(X_train)))\n    cal_idx, fit_idx = idx[:n_cal], idx[n_cal:]\n    X_fit, y_fit = X_train[fit_idx], y_train[fit_idx]\n    X_cal, y_cal = X_train[cal_idx], y_train[cal_idx]\n    if len(np.unique(y_fit)) < 2 or len(np.unique(y_cal)) < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"degenerate fit/calibration split\")\n\n    ctx_idx = rng.choice(len(X_fit), size=min(context_size, len(X_fit)), replace=False)\n    X_ctx, y_ctx = X_fit[ctx_idx], y_fit[ctx_idx]\n    if len(np.unique(y_ctx)) < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"degenerate context\")\n\n    proba_cal = run_tabpfn(X_ctx, y_ctx, X_cal)\n    weights_cal, _ = compute_domain_weights(X_cal, X_target_unlabeled, seed=seed)\n\n    eps = 1e-6\n    logits_cal = np.log(np.clip(proba_cal, eps, 1 - eps) / np.clip(1 - proba_cal, eps, 1 - eps)).reshape(-1, 1)\n    platt = LogisticRegression()\n    platt.fit(logits_cal, y_cal, sample_weight=weights_cal)\n\n    proba_test_raw = run_tabpfn(X_ctx, y_ctx, X_score)\n    logits_test = np.log(np.clip(proba_test_raw, eps, 1 - eps) / np.clip(1 - proba_test_raw, eps, 1 - eps)).reshape(-1, 1)\n    return platt.predict_proba(logits_test)[:, 1]\n\nprint(\"Models + metrics ready. TabPFN device:\", TABPFN_DEVICE)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-12T21:09:38.646882Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-12T21:09:38.647192Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-12T21:09:42.967931Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-12T21:09:38.647171Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-12T21:09:42.967225Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"[device check] CUDA reported available but a test op failed (AcceleratorError: CUDA error: no kernel image is available for execution on the device\nSearch for `cudaErrorNoKernelImageForDevice' in https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-runtime-api/group__CUDART__TYPES.html for more information.\nCUDA kernel errors might be asynchronously reported at some other API call, so the stacktrace below might be incorrect.\nFor debugging consider passing CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1\nCompile with `TORCH_USE_CUDA_DSA` to enable device-side assertions.\n); falling back to CPU.\nTabPFN will run on: cpu\nModels + metrics ready. TabPFN device: cpu\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":8},{"id":"38e4d511-4d37-4c4d-b4aa-f4b7def89697","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 5. Main experiment loop\n\nSame grid structure as v1, extended with: the new baselines, the `domain_shift_auc` diagnostic logged\nper split (used in Section 7's mechanism analysis), and now runs on all 5 datasets (electricity\nparticipates in the synthetic grid too, in addition to its dedicated chronological case study in\nSection 6b).\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"e062fd0f-22eb-4b10-afa7-0dbd4cd8ab25","cell_type":"code","source":"QUICK_TEST = True  # <-- flip to False for the full run\n\nif QUICK_TEST:\n    CONTEXT_SIZES = [300]\n    SEVERITIES_RUN = [0.0, 1.0]\n    N_SEEDS_PER_CONFIG = 1\n    DATASETS_RUN = DATASETS[:2]\nelse:\n    CONTEXT_SIZES = [200, 500, 1000]\n    SEVERITIES_RUN = SEVERITIES\n    N_SEEDS_PER_CONFIG = 3\n    DATASETS_RUN = DATASETS\n\nTARGET_UNLABELED_FRACTION = 0.3\nCALIBRATION_CONTEXT_SIZE = 500  # fixed context size used by the reweighted-calibration baseline\n\n# ---- resume-from-checkpoint: if results_raw.csv already has rows for a (dataset, shift_type,\n# severity, seed) config, skip re-running that whole config. This matters because a Kaggle session\n# can time out (9hr limit) or restart partway through the full grid — without this, a restart means\n# re-running everything, including hours of already-completed TabPFN calls. ----\nRESUME_FROM_CHECKPOINT = True\n\nif RESUME_FROM_CHECKPOINT and os.path.exists(RESULTS_PATH):\n    _prev = pd.read_csv(RESULTS_PATH)\n    _prev_ok = _prev[_prev[\"status\"] == \"ok\"]\n    completed_configs = set(\n        _prev_ok[[\"dataset\", \"shift_type\", \"severity\", \"seed\"]]\n        .apply(lambda r: (r[\"dataset\"], r[\"shift_type\"], round(float(r[\"severity\"]), 6), int(r[\"seed\"])), axis=1)\n    )\n    results = _prev.to_dict(\"records\")\n    print(f\"Resuming: found {len(_prev)} existing rows ({len(completed_configs)} completed configs) in {RESULTS_PATH}\")\nelse:\n    completed_configs = set()\n    results = []\n\ndef log_result(**kwargs):\n    results.append(kwargs)\n\ndef timed_call(fn):\n    \"\"\"Runs fn(), returns (result, elapsed_seconds). Lets us report per-method wall-clock cost —\n    the actual number the 'lightweight, no retraining' claim needs, not just an assertion.\"\"\"\n    t0 = time.time()\n    out = fn()\n    return out, time.time() - t0\n\ntotal_start = time.time()\n\nfor spec in DATASETS_RUN:\n    print(f\"\\n=== Dataset: {spec.name} ===\")\n    try:\n        X_raw, y = load_dataset(spec)\n        shift_vals = X_raw[spec.shift_feature].astype(float).values\n        X_proc, feat_names = preprocess(X_raw)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"  [SKIP dataset] {spec.name}: {e}\")\n        log_result(dataset=spec.name, shift_type=None, severity=None, strategy=None,\n                   context_size=None, seed=None, status=\"failed_load\", error=str(e), elapsed_seconds=None)\n        continue\n\n    for shift_type, builder in SHIFT_BUILDERS.items():\n        for severity in SEVERITIES_RUN:\n            for seed in range(N_SEEDS_PER_CONFIG):\n                run_seed = SEED + seed\n                config_key = (spec.name, shift_type, round(float(severity), 6), run_seed)\n                if config_key in completed_configs:\n                    print(f\"  [SKIP, already done] {shift_type} severity={severity} seed={run_seed}\")\n                    continue\n                try:\n                    if shift_type == \"covariate\":\n                        X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test = builder(X_proc, y, shift_vals, severity, seed=run_seed)\n                    else:\n                        X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test = builder(X_proc, y, severity, seed=run_seed)\n\n                    if len(np.unique(y_train)) < 2 or len(np.unique(y_test)) < 2:\n                        raise ValueError(\"degenerate split: only one class present\")\n\n                    rng = np.random.RandomState(run_seed)\n                    n_test = len(X_test)\n                    n_unlabeled = max(10, int(n_test * TARGET_UNLABELED_FRACTION))\n                    perm = rng.permutation(n_test)\n                    unlabeled_idx, score_idx = perm[:n_unlabeled], perm[n_unlabeled:]\n                    X_target_unlabeled = X_test[unlabeled_idx]\n                    X_score, y_score = X_test[score_idx], y_test[score_idx]\n                    if len(np.unique(y_score)) < 2:\n                        raise ValueError(\"degenerate scoring split\")\n\n                    try:\n                        _, domain_shift_auc = compute_domain_weights(X_train, X_target_unlabeled, seed=run_seed)\n                    except Exception:\n                        domain_shift_auc = np.nan\n\n                    common = dict(dataset=spec.name, shift_type=shift_type, severity=severity,\n                                  seed=run_seed, domain_shift_auc=domain_shift_auc)\n\n                    # ---- full-data / retraining baselines ----\n                    baseline_fns = {\n                        \"xgboost_full\": lambda: run_xgb_full(X_train, y_train, X_score),\n                        \"random_forest_full\": lambda: run_rf_full(X_train, y_train, X_score),\n                        \"lightgbm_full\": lambda: run_lgbm_full(X_train, y_train, X_score),\n                        \"xgboost_importance_weighted\": lambda: run_xgb_importance_weighted(\n                            X_train, y_train, X_score, X_target_unlabeled=X_target_unlabeled, seed=run_seed),\n                    }\n                    for bname, fn in baseline_fns.items():\n                        try:\n                            proba, elapsed = timed_call(fn)\n                            metrics = score_predictions(y_score, proba)\n                            log_result(**common, strategy=bname, context_size=len(X_train),\n                                       status=\"ok\", error=None, elapsed_seconds=elapsed, **metrics)\n                        except Exception as e:\n                            log_result(**common, strategy=bname, context_size=len(X_train),\n                                       status=\"failed\", error=f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}\", elapsed_seconds=None)\n\n                    # ---- TabPFN + reweighted calibration baseline (fixed context size) ----\n                    try:\n                        proba, elapsed = timed_call(lambda: run_tabpfn_reweighted_calibration(\n                            X_train, y_train, X_target_unlabeled, X_score,\n                            context_size=CALIBRATION_CONTEXT_SIZE, seed=run_seed))\n                        metrics = score_predictions(y_score, proba)\n                        log_result(**common, strategy=\"tabpfn_reweighted_calibration\",\n                                   context_size=CALIBRATION_CONTEXT_SIZE, status=\"ok\", error=None,\n                                   elapsed_seconds=elapsed, **metrics)\n                    except Exception as e:\n                        log_result(**common, strategy=\"tabpfn_reweighted_calibration\",\n                                   context_size=CALIBRATION_CONTEXT_SIZE, status=\"failed\",\n                                   error=f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}\", elapsed_seconds=None)\n\n                    # ---- TabPFN under each context strategy x context size ----\n                    for context_size in CONTEXT_SIZES:\n                        for strategy_name, strategy_fn in CONTEXT_STRATEGIES.items():\n                            try:\n                                def _run():\n                                    idx = strategy_fn(X_train, y_train, X_target_unlabeled, context_size, seed=run_seed)\n                                    X_ctx, y_ctx = X_train[idx], y_train[idx]\n                                    if len(np.unique(y_ctx)) < 2:\n                                        raise ValueError(\"context has only one class; skipping\")\n                                    return run_tabpfn(X_ctx, y_ctx, X_score)\n                                proba, elapsed = timed_call(_run)\n                                metrics = score_predictions(y_score, proba)\n                                log_result(**common, strategy=strategy_name, context_size=context_size,\n                                           status=\"ok\", error=None, elapsed_seconds=elapsed, **metrics)\n                            except Exception as e:\n                                log_result(**common, strategy=strategy_name, context_size=context_size,\n                                           status=\"failed\", error=f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}\", elapsed_seconds=None)\n\n                    print(f\"  {shift_type} severity={severity} seed={run_seed}: done (shift_auc={domain_shift_auc:.3f})\")\n\n                except Exception as e:\n                    print(f\"  [SKIP config] {shift_type} severity={severity} seed={run_seed}: {e}\")\n                    log_result(dataset=spec.name, shift_type=shift_type, severity=severity, seed=run_seed,\n                               strategy=None, context_size=None, domain_shift_auc=np.nan, elapsed_seconds=None,\n                               status=\"failed_split\", error=f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}\")\n\n                pd.DataFrame(results).to_csv(RESULTS_PATH, index=False)\n\nprint(f\"\\nTotal time: {(time.time() - total_start)/60:.1f} min\")\nprint(f\"Saved {len(results)} rows to {RESULTS_PATH}\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-12T21:09:42.969312Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-12T21:09:42.969905Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-12T21:11:10.971598Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-12T21:09:42.96988Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-12T21:11:10.970686Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"\n=== Dataset: adult_income ===\n  covariate severity=0.0 seed=42: done (shift_auc=0.500)\n  covariate severity=1.0 seed=42: done (shift_auc=1.000)\n  label severity=0.0 seed=42: done (shift_auc=0.509)\n  label severity=1.0 seed=42: done (shift_auc=0.561)\n  feature_noise severity=0.0 seed=42: done (shift_auc=0.514)\n  feature_noise severity=1.0 seed=42: done (shift_auc=0.504)\n\n=== Dataset: german_credit ===\n  covariate severity=0.0 seed=42: done (shift_auc=0.484)\n  covariate severity=1.0 seed=42: done (shift_auc=0.992)\n  label severity=0.0 seed=42: done (shift_auc=0.598)\n  label severity=1.0 seed=42: done (shift_auc=0.514)\n  feature_noise severity=0.0 seed=42: done (shift_auc=0.511)\n  feature_noise severity=1.0 seed=42: done (shift_auc=0.534)\n\nTotal time: 1.5 min\nSaved 120 rows to results_raw.csv\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":9},{"id":"9fce1ad7-f0bd-47e0-97a0-882c06b08844","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 6a. Sanity check the main run","metadata":{}},{"id":"d740ed0e-b917-49d5-85c8-6e7334a0b766","cell_type":"code","source":"df = pd.read_csv(RESULTS_PATH)\nprint(\"Total rows:\", len(df))\nprint(df[\"status\"].value_counts())\nfailed = df[df[\"status\"] != \"ok\"]\nif len(failed):\n    print(\"\\nFailure breakdown by dataset / shift_type / strategy:\")\n    print(failed.groupby([\"dataset\", \"shift_type\", \"strategy\"], dropna=False).size().sort_values(ascending=False).head(20))\n    print(\"\\nSample error messages:\")\n    print(failed[\"error\"].dropna().unique()[:10])\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.b