id":"ba370ace-2514-4c3d-b154-3bc885b90be9","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 8. Mechanism analysis — does context curation help more when shift is more detectable?\n\n`domain_shift_auc` (logged per split during the main loop) is a cheap, unlabeled-only estimate of \"how\nseparable is train from target.\" If `shift_aware_reweight`'s benefit over `random` **grows** with this\ndiagnostic, that's a mechanistic story worth a full figure/table in the paper, not just an average\nacross all severities pooled together. If it **doesn't**, that's also worth reporting honestly — it\nwould mean the benefit is more about class-balance or coverage effects than shift-awareness per se.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"8c302919-45a1-44bf-a6ba-73e838e4b4ea","cell_type":"code","source":"merge_cols = [\"dataset\", \"shift_type\", \"severity\", \"seed\", \"context_size\"]\nwide = ok[ok[\"strategy\"].isin([\"random\", \"shift_aware_reweight\"])].pivot_table(\n    index=merge_cols, columns=\"strategy\", values=\"accuracy\"\n).dropna()\nshift_auc_lookup = ok.drop_duplicates(subset=[\"dataset\", \"shift_type\", \"severity\", \"seed\"])[\n    [\"dataset\", \"shift_type\", \"severity\", \"seed\", \"domain_shift_auc\"]\n]\nwide = wide.reset_index().merge(shift_auc_lookup, on=[\"dataset\", \"shift_type\", \"severity\", \"seed\"], how=\"left\")\nwide[\"benefit\"] = wide[\"shift_aware_reweight\"] - wide[\"random\"]\n\nif len(wide) > 5:\n    corr = wide[[\"domain_shift_auc\", \"benefit\"]].corr().iloc[0, 1]\n    print(f\"Correlation between domain-shift AUC and shift_aware_reweight's benefit over random: {corr:.3f}\")\n\n    plt.figure(figsize=(6, 5))\n    sns.regplot(data=wide, x=\"domain_shift_auc\", y=\"benefit\", scatter_kws={\"alpha\": 0.5})\n    plt.axhline(0, color=\"gray\", linestyle=\"--\", linewidth=1)\n    plt.xlabel(\"Domain-classifier shift-detectability AUC (unlabeled-only diagnostic)\")\n    plt.ylabel(\"Accuracy benefit of shift_aware_reweight over random\")\n    plt.title(\"Does context 